WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:01.410
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:06.289
Let's start with something positive, we have
genuinely better and better looking COVID

00:00:06.289 --> 00:00:12.170
updates over the last few weeks globally and
in the United States, and today is no exception.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.099
Questions we're asking right now before we
look at the data.

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:16.330
Is this the last wave?

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.730
We don't know.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.289
What will the winter look like?

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:20.600
We're not yet sure.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.730
How much more do we need to vaccinate?

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.480
Quite a bit, but we're not totally sure.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.130
Many other questions as well.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:32.500
Let's start with cases since the daily Delta
variant peak of about one hundred and 67000

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.570
cases per day.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:40.129
The United States is now down 39 percent in
daily average cases to about one hundred and

00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:44.079
2000 per day outrageously high.

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:48.399
But as more and more people get vaccinated,
cases will mean less and less.

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:52.040
Dr. Isaac Bogoch last week told us, but we're
not there yet.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:59.629
And for now, 39 percent daily case reduction
is a very good thing in terms of deaths in

00:00:59.629 --> 00:01:00.629
general.

00:01:00.629 --> 00:01:05.130
You know this by now, rule of thumb deaths
follow cases by three to four weeks.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.720
Deaths are continuing to do so.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:13.510
Deaths now down about 20 percent per day from
their Delta peak.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:17.150
The Delta Peak was about 9500 deaths per day.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:20.160
We're now down to about 6500 deaths per day.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.200
Still a really high number.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:27.120
Remember that a typical flu season is about
36000 deaths a year.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.470
That's like 100 deaths a day.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:37.480
So right now, we're at 16 times a typical
flu seasons, daily deaths 16 times.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.180
That's an interesting metric, by the way,
to compare when we think about the relative

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.650
risk of death from COVID when we're out there.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.570
How does this compare to a flu season over
the course of a year?

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:52.420
And the truth is, it's not really like this
because you're 36000 flu deaths are concentrated

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.800
during flu season.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.020
That's why we call it flu season.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:59.560
But on average, 100 flu deaths a day is what
the U.S. sees in a year.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.960
We're now at 6500 COVID deaths per day.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:09.200
Globally, we are seeing cases continuing down
about 35 percent since the Delta Peak.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.840
And then, of course, global deaths as well
have peaked at about ten thousand three hundred

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:14.840
a day.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:18.210
Those are now down to about 7000 global deaths
a day.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:24.050
That's a reduction of about a third, 31 percent
to be exact in daily global deaths.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:26.010
So that's good.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.110
Now how about vaccination?

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:32.480
Well, as we talked about last week or the
week before, the U.S. is getting embarrassed.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:37.440
The U.S. is rapidly declining in terms of
the percentage of people vaccinated in the

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:43.720
U.S. compared to other countries, particularly
compared to other so-called rich countries.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.480
Take a look at this.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:52.750
The leaders in vaccinated percentage are the
United Arab Emirates tiny country, followed

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:58.770
by Portugal, which has 10 million people Chile,
Spain, Singapore, Uruguay, Canada, Denmark,

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:04.400
China, Ireland, Italy, Finland, France, Japan,
U.K., Brazil, Germany.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:09.670
Then you get to the United States in vaccinated
percentage just ahead of Turkey.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.890
And just ahead of Mexico.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.420
What happened to us?

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:19.240
We had all the vaccines earlier than anyone,
and we just can't do it.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.650
People aren't getting the vaccine.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.130
It's horrifying what's going on.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:26.040
It's embarrassing what's going on, and we've
talked about it so much.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:31.660
And then lastly, the global vaccination effort
overall has also slowed down.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:38.130
Globally, we had gotten up to about 45 million
vaccines per day around the world.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:43.280
We're now down to roughly half of that, about
23 million vaccine doses per day.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:50.730
If you look at the global population, that
means each day we're vaccinating 0.2 nine

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:54.050
percent of the global population call it zero
point three.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:04:00.900
Just under a third of one percent of the world
is getting a dose each day, getting that back

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.430
up to 45 million doses a day.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.720
Even 50 60 million doses a day would be absolutely
huge.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.770
But the good news?

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.470
No thanks to the deniers.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:16.389
No thanks to the anti-vaxxers and those spreading
the disinformation and misinformation cases

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.820
down significantly.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.169
Deaths also down.

00:04:20.169 --> 00:04:21.660
Let's hope it continues.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:56.230
We'll check in next week and hope that the
numbers are looking 

00:04:56.230 --> 00:05:25.350
even better.

